stance with Z Clip Scale enabled causes lag spike, only when SubViewport with camera is present.\n\nPutting assigned material to a variable seems to stop lag spikes from happening, even after creating another mesh instance from scratch.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a MeshInstance3D with meshes.\n2. Assign StandardMaterial3D with `use_z_clip_scale = true` to mesh instance.\n3. Add mesh instance to scene tree.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[z_clip_scale_lag_test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28341369/z_clip_scale_lag_test.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119845/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119845/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"reopened","pinned_comment":null}